⟦ classification_policy_plan | CLASSIFICATION-POLICY-PLAN-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-08-17T07:39:04Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status active
// plan/classification-policy-plan-v1/classification_policy_plan.vsm — the FORMAL plan to create the
// DOCUMENT-CLASSIFICATION POLICY: the binary decision tree (Socratic
// questionnaire) that maps every .vsm under docs/spec_revision/ to its
// canonical directory. GENERIC: the tree is the policy; any future
// directory/doc is classified by applying the questionnaire until no
// higher level of classification remains — which is the same as saying
// "until the directory is reached".
//
// Status lives in TASKS.vsm (doc_sync discipline). This doc is the
// framing/rationale/strategy — the WHY and the HOW, not the status.
//
// S5 rmw3, 2026-08-17: "cualquier tarea de clasificación se transforma en
// la aplicación de un cuestionario... hasta que no pueda subir más niveles
// de clasificación, que es lo mismo que directorios." (trans. from ES)
// The questionnaire IS the tree IS the directory hierarchy. The policy
// MUST materialize as an instrument (check/daemon) and enter the automated
// cycle so every action satisfies all formal requirements, and every doc
// can withstand changes in the system's specifications.

// ─── PART I — PRINCIPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

principle:
  "Classification is the application of a questionnaire. The questionnaire
   is a binary decision tree: start from ONE boolean about the NATURE of
   the document (not its destination — Socratic, non-leading), branch by
   answering, until no higher level of classification remains. The leaf
   IS the directory. A directory is a category; every document belongs to
   exactly one category; orphans are violations."

  // Why Socratic (S5 rmw3, 2026-08-17):
  //   - a leading question ('is it a spec? → spec/') presumes the answer
  //     it wants; the tree must ask about WHAT THE DOCUMENT IS, not where
  //     it should go
  //   - dialectic: each node confronts two poles (norm vs state, rule vs
  //     specification, present vs past) and the document's nature decides
  //   - the tree is the taxonomy; the taxonomy is the directory schema;
  //     ONE source, no duplicated functions (A6 — no parallel organs)
  //
  // Why an instrument (S5 rmw3, 2026-08-17):
  //   - the policy must materialize as a check/daemon and enter the
  //     automated cycle (write-time hook + pre-commit gate)
  //   - every action (write, move, promote, archive) must satisfy all
  //     formal requirements — the instrument enforces, the agent corrects,
  //     the commit verifies (R18 autonomy of the cycle)
  //   - documents must RESIST changes in the system's specifications:
  //     the canonical version of the tree lives in THIS doc (and its
  //     ratified successor in system/), the instrument READS it
  //     parametrically — a tree change re-classifies without editing
  //     every check (same pattern as version-change-plan: canonical read
  //     from primer, parametric checks)

// ─── PART II — THE TREE (THE QUESTIONNAIRE) ────────────────────────────────

questionnaire: "
  NODO 0 — ¿El documento AFIRMA cómo debe ser el mundo (declara norma),
           o DOCUMENTA cómo es/está/fue (registra estado)?
  │
  ├── NORMA ─────────────────────────────── NODO 1
  │   └─ ¿REGLA de comportamiento (quién puede qué)
  │      o ESPECIFICACIÓN de construcción (cómo se hace)?
  │      ├─ REGLA → system/<órgano>/        (política, axioma, protocolo)
  │      └─ ESPECIFICACIÓN → NODO 2
  │          └─ ¿describe un INSTRUMENTO que corre (script/check/plugin)
  │             o una INVESTIGACIÓN (experimento/eje)?
  │             ├─ INSTRUMENTO → design-sources/     (R16)
  │             └─ INVESTIGACIÓN → NODO 3
  │                 └─ ¿tiene PLAN padre activo?
  │                    ├─ SÍ → plan/<plan>/<fase>/    (spec dentro del plan)
  │                    └─ NO → sandbox/ hasta engancharse a un plan
  │                            (spec sin plan = VIOLACIÓN, nunca huérfano)
  │
  └── ESTADO ────────────────────────────── NODO 4
      └─ ¿PRESENTE (vigente, en curso) o PASADO (cumplido)?
         ├─ PASADO → archive/<clase>/       (indexado, citado por linaje)
         └─ PRESENTE → NODO 5
             └─ ¿REGISTRO de evento u OPERACIÓN del árbol?
                ├─ EVENTO → NODO 6
                │   └─ ¿INCIDENTE (falló) o APRENDIZAJE (lección)?
                │      ├─ INCIDENTE → incidents/
                │      └─ APRENDIZAJE → learning_records/
                ├─ OPERACIÓN/contabilidad → ledger/   (censo, worklist, ledger)
                └─ MATERIAL DE TRABAJO → NODO 7
                    └─ ¿PLAN (objetivo+fases) o PROPUESTA (idea sin validar)?
                       ├─ PLAN → plan/       (árbol, ver PART III)
                       └─ PROPUESTA → sandbox/
"

  // The tree IS the questionnaire: applying it to any document produces
  // its canonical directory. Terminal nodes = leaves = directories.
  // A document whose questionnaire path ends in a directory IS classified;
  // a document whose path cannot complete (no leaf) is an orphan —
  // violation. The instrument (PART IV) automates this application.

// ─── PART III — plan/ AS A TREE (S5 rmw3 2026-08-17) ───────────────────────

plan_tree:
  "A spec is normally part of a plan — there should be NO spec without a
   plan. Therefore a plan is a FOLDER with a root document, and specs live
   in SUBFOLDERS that define the plan's phases or stages:

   plan/
   ├── README.vsm            gateway
   ├── plans_active.vsm      TRUNK — fractal index: ALL plans, their phases
   │                         and stages, and every task recognizable from
   │                         plan/ (tension TASKS↔plan: declared, not yet
   │                         resolved — plan as tree; trunk indexes all
   │                         plans with phases/stages fractally; tasks
   │                         should be recognizable from plan/)
   ├── <plan-01>/
   │   ├── root.vsm          the plan's root document (objective + phases)
   │   ├── phase-01/
   │   │   ├── spec_a.vsm    specs INSIDE the phase
   │   │   └── ...
   │   └── phase-02/ ...
   └── <plan-02>/ ...

   Lifecycle of a plan (maximum synthesis):
     plan active → (phases executed) → COMPLETE:
       1. synthesis to system/ — the MAXIMUM possible: a doc, a block, or
          even ONE LINE inside an existing doc (never duplicate what was
          absorbed; 'lo que busco es que pase la mayor síntesis posible' —
          trans. from ES, S5 rmw3 2026-08-17)
       2. the rest of the plan → archive/superseded/ with an INDEX entry
"

  // Tension TASKS↔plan: S5 rmw3 2026-08-17 — 'no creo que para resolver
  // ahora... pero si plan es un árbol, en el tronco de plan deberían estar
  // indexados todos los planes con sus respectivas fases y etapas de manera
  // fractalizada... entonces todas las tareas deberían ser posibles
  // reconocerlas desde plan/.' (trans. from ES) — DECLARED, deferred.

// ─── PART IV — THE INSTRUMENT (MATERIALIZATION) ────────────────────────────

instrument:
  "The policy materializes as a check that applies the questionnaire:

   checks/classification-valid [pass|fail]
     pass -> for every .vsm under docs/spec_revision/ (or staged files),
             apply the questionnaire by reading the document's declared
             nature (header, @status, @type, role); the leaf directory
             MUST equal the document's actual directory. Exit 0.
     fail -> deliberately-false variant: a misplaced doc is asserted to
             pass (must exit non-zero — false claim fails).

   The tree is READ FROM this plan doc (and its ratified successor in
   system/) — parametric, never hard-coded in the check. A tree change
   re-classifies without editing the check (R16: instrument interprets,
   policy declares).

   Integration in the automated cycle:
     - write-time daemon (vsl-check-on-write): classification check joins
       grammar/encoding/version — advisory for half-written docs, BLOCKING
       for a doc written outside its canonical category
     - pre-commit gate: checks/classification-valid BLOCKS a commit that
       stages a doc in the wrong directory (extends dir-schema-valid's
       role: the tree IS the schema's ontology, one source)
     - archive-index-valid: archive/ coverage already BLOCKS orphans
       (built 2026-08-17) — the tree generalizes the same principle to
       every directory
"

  // Resilience to specification change: the tree lives in the CANON
  // (this plan → system/ when ratified), the instrument READS it. A doc
  // already classified by the old tree is re-classified by the new one
  // without touching the check — the document resists the change because
  // its category is a function of its NATURE, not of its history.



// ─── PART IV-B — THE TREE AS MACHINE-READABLE RULES (classify.py reads this) ─
// The Socratic questionnaire as a declarative rule table. classify.py
// (scripts/vsl/classify.py) READS this table — it is the single source of
// truth for the deterministic leaves; a tree change re-classifies without
// editing the instrument (R16 parametric pattern). Each rule maps a type
// pattern (+optional @status) to its canonical directory. The ASCII tree
// in PART II is the human-readable rendering of THIS table.
tree_rules: [
  // ── REGLAS ESPECÍFICAS PRIMERO (orden = prioridad: la primera que matchea gana)
  // ESTADO → PASADO → archive/<clase>/ (registro histórico — @status
  // historical_record|archived — las mediciones/ejemplos/superados usan archived)
  rule("ESTADO-PASADO", type="*ARCHIVE*|*THEORY-CL-*|*BOOT-COHERENCE*|*RESTRUCT-SURVEY*|*VSM-LOGIC-DEMO*", status="archived", home="archive"),
  // ESTADO → PASADO → archive/ — con @status historical_record (THEORY-DYN etc)
  rule("ESTADO-PASADO-HR", type="*THEORY-*|*BOOT-COHERENCE*|*PH-00-*", status="historical_record", home="archive"),
  rule("ARCHIVE-INDEX", type="*ARCHIVE-index*", home="archive"),
  rule("ARCHIVE-README", type="*ARCHIVE-readme*", home="archive"),
  rule("DESIGN-SOURCES-INDEX", type="*DESIGN-SOURCES-index*", home="design-sources"),
  rule("DESIGN-SOURCES-README", type="*DESIGN-SOURCES-readme*", home="design-sources"),
  rule("LEDGER-README", type="*LEDGER-readme*", home="ledger"),
  rule("PLAN-README", type="*PLAN-readme*", home="plan"),
  rule("EXP-ARDUINO-S1", type="*exp-arduino-s1*", home="plan"),
  rule("EXP-TOKEN-GROUNDING", type="*exp-token-grounding*", home="plan"),
  rule("ROOT-README", type="*SPEC-REVISION-readme*", home="."),
  rule("SANDBOX-README", type="*SANDBOX-readme*", home="sandbox"),
  rule("SYSTEM-README", type="*SYSTEM-readme*", home="system"),
  rule("S5-POLICY-README", type="*S5-POLICY-README*", home="system"),
  rule("SANDBOX-README", type="*SANDBOX-README*", home="sandbox"),
  // ESTADO → PRESENTE → OPERACIÓN → ledger/
  rule("ESTADO-OPERACION", type="*CENSUS*|*WORKLIST*|*LEDGER*", home="ledger"),
  // ESTADO → EVENTO → INCIDENTE → incidents/
  rule("ESTADO-INCIDENTE", type="*INCIDENT*", home="incidents"),
  // ESTADO → EVENTO → APRENDIZAJE → learning_records/
  rule("ESTADO-APRENDIZAJE", type="*LEARNING-RECORD*", home="learning_records"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO → design-sources/ (validado/promovido)
  // — ANTES de MATERIAL-PLAN: *PLAN-TREE-DESIGN* contiene DESIGN (design-source)
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-INSTRUMENTO", type="*DESIGN*|*RUBRIC*", home="design-sources"),
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-DESIGN-SPEC", type="*DESIGN-SPEC*", home="design-sources"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — design-source types específicos
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-DESIGN-SOURCE", type="*DIR-SCHEMA*|*SYSTEM-MAP*|*RELOCATE-VSM*|*RELOCATE-GATE*|*PLUGIN-AUDIT*|*PLUGIN-CLASS-TAXONOMY*|*STRUCTURAL-INTEGRITY-CHECKS*|*PLUGIN-MODEL-ANALYSIS-v1*|*SCRIPTS-REORGANIZATION-PROPOSAL-v1*|*DRIVER-TOPOLOGY*|*TOOL-AUTONOMY*|*PATTERN-RUNNER*|*SECOND-ORDER-LOOP*|*CANONICAL*", home="design-sources"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — R16-SPEC (design source)
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-R16", type="*R16*", home="design-sources"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — specs en validación (@status design)
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-DESIGN-SANDBOX", type="*SPEC*", status="design", home="sandbox"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INVESTIGACIÓN (experimento/eje). NODO 3: ¿tiene PLAN
  // padre activo? SÍ → plan/<plan>/<fase>/ (spec dentro del plan — declarado
  // como fase/spec de un plan; classify.py resuelve consultando los planes);
  // NO → sandbox/ hasta engancharse a un plan (spec sin plan = VIOLACIÓN,
  // nunca huérfano).
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-INVESTIGACION", type="*AXIS2*|*EXP-*", plan_parent="true", home="plan"),
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-INVESTIGACION-SIN-PLAN", type="*AXIS2*|*EXP-*", home="sandbox"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/plan/ — excepcion exacta: el plan estrategico
  // canonico vive en system/plan/ por decision S5 (CODE1 remediation).
  // TYPE exacto PLAN-v1 SIN comodin: no captura CLASSIFICATION-POLICY-PLAN-v1
  // ni VERSION-CHANGE-PLAN-v1 (fnmatch exacto). La cadena sigue en
  // system/classification.local.vsm (CAT-plan-v1 → plan) y cierra en
  // system/plan/classification.local.vsm (CAT-strategy-plan → ".").
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-PLAN-SISTEMA", type="PLAN-v1", home="system"),
  // ESTADO → PRESENTE → MATERIAL → PLAN → plan/ (incluye planes de teoría:
  // THEORY-HRS/SID/SB — h_rest_senescence, seven_ideas_deep, symbiogenesis_lab)
  rule("MATERIAL-PLAN", type="*PLAN*|*ARC-TREE*|*REVISION-PLAN*|*CLASSIFICATION-POLICY*|*THEORY-HRS*|*THEORY-SID*|*THEORY-SB*", home="plan"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ (política, axioma, protocolo)
  rule("NORMA-REGLA", type="*POLICY*|*RULES*|*COVENANT*|*AXIOM*|*PROTOCOL*|*S5-*|*AGENT-WRITE-GATES*|*AGENT-INSTRUMENTS*|*LEARNING-CYCLE-POLICY*", home="system"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ — types de órganos del sistema. Patrones
  // PRECISOS (un type de órgano con @status proposed = en revisión DENTRO del
  // canon, NO propuesta sandbox). fnmatch: *S1-CONTRACT* NO matchea
  // S1-BBH-CONTRACT-01 — se usan patrones con comodín en el prefijo de órgano.
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-ORGANO", type="*S1-*-CONTRACT*|*S1-*-INSTANCE*|*S2-NATS*|*S3-ALLOCATION*|*S3STAR-*|*S4-*|*THEORY-LR*|*KERNEL-*|*INFRA-01*|*INST-VALIDATION*|*VSF-INSTANCE-v*|*VSL-CORE*|*VSL-LANG*|*VSL-HARD*|*VSL-REGULATION*|*VSL-AGENT*", home="system"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ — teoría del kernel/sistema activa
  // (THEORY-01/02 kernel, THEORY-VC/AP/S4L conjecture, THEORY-DVP ratified)
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-THEORY-ACTIVE", type="*THEORY-*", status="active", home="system"),
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-THEORY-OTHER", type="*THEORY-VC*|*THEORY-AP*|*THEORY-S4L*|*THEORY-DVP*|*THEORY-01*|*THEORY-02*|*THEORY-DYN*", home="system"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ — templates de instancias y specs S1
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-TEMPLATES", type="*VSF-INST-TPL-*", home="system"),
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-S1-SPEC", type="*S1-01*|*S1-SPEC*", home="system"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ — mapa de agentes (s5-policy)
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-AGENT-MAP", type="*AGENT-MAP*|*AGENT-INSTRUMENTS*", home="system"),
  // ESTADO → APRENDIZAJE → learning_records/ (propuestas de ciclo de aprendizaje)
  rule("ESTADO-APRENDIZAJE-PROPUESTA", type="*LEARNING-CYCLE*|*LEARNING-RECORD*", home="learning_records"),
  // NORMA → REGLA → system/<órgano>/ — boot canon y ontology (types con
  // patrón ONTOLOGY/BOOT que NO son propuestas sandbox — @status ratified)
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-BOOT", type="*BOOT-*|*ONTOLOGY-*", status="ratified", home="system"),
  // ESTADO → PRESENTE → MATERIAL → PROPUESTA → sandbox/ (proposed sin validar)
  // — catch-all SOLO para types no cubiertos arriba
  rule("MATERIAL-PROPUESTA", type="*", status="proposed", home="sandbox"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — agent evaluation battery (sandbox)
  rule("AGENT-EVAL-BATTERY", type="*AGENT-EVAL-BATTERY*|*LIVE-TEST*", home="sandbox"),
  // NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — agent layer status report (sandbox)
  rule("AGENT-LAYER-STATUS-REPORT", type="*AGENT-LAYER-STATUS-REPORT*", home="sandbox"),
  // ── NORMA → REGLA → system/s1-operations — parent WIP types (rsi_*, etc.)
  // classified to their existing dirs (dir_schema.spec.vsm already claims
  // them). R7 model==reality: the directory is the source of truth.
  rule("NORMA-REGLA-S1-OPS-WIP", type="*MANIFEST-v1*|*RESULTS-v1*|*ROADMAP-v1*|*ARCHITECTURE-v1*", home="system"),
  rule("ESTADO-INSTANCE-WIP", type="*SCRIPTS-STATE-MANIFEST-v1*", home="system"),
  // ── NORMA → ESPEC → INSTRUMENTO — parent WIP design-sources analyses
  rule("NORMA-ESPEC-DESIGN-WIP", type="*PLUGIN-MODEL-ANALYSIS-v1*|*SCRIPTS-REORGANIZATION-PROPOSAL-v1*", home="design-sources"),
]

// ─── PART V — IMPLEMENTATION STEPS ─────────────────────────────────────────

steps: [
  "S1 — remove system/sandbox/ (phantom, empty, no live references — A1
        verified 2026-08-17; only historical mentions in docs/archive and
        child/docs/deploy)",
  "S2 — create design-sources/ at spec_revision/ level 1 (README gateway +
        INDEX + dir_schema declaration + BLOCKING coverage check); move the
        3 current design-sources OUT of system/s5-policy/agent-policy/
        (PLUGIN-AUDIT-DESIGN, RELOCATE-GATE-SPEC, RELOCATE-VSM-SPEC) +
        normalize names to kebab-case; update checks/impl-with-design-valid
        (DESIGN_DIRS), hard_rules R16, git_pre_commit.sh, s5-policy README,
        agent_instruments.vsm",
  "S3 — reclassify the 7 root orphans (PART II application):
        certification_rubric → system/; instance_layer_proposal → sandbox/;
        revision_plan → plan/; census_docs + worklist_vsl → ledger/;
        ph00_boot_coherence_review → archive/superseded/; dir_schema +
        system_map → design-sources/; axis2_* + EXP-* → plan/<plan>/<fase>/",
  "S4 — restructure plan/ as a tree: trunk (plans_active.vsm fractal index),
        each plan a folder with root.vsm + phase-*/ subfolders holding its
        specs; lifecycle synthesis-to-system on completion",
  "S5 — build checks/classification-valid (tree read from this doc,
        parametric; negative control); integrate write-time + pre-commit;
        full census of broken routes (paths referenced ≠ paths existing)
        and repair",
]

// ─── PART VI — VERIFICATION / GATES ────────────────────────────────────────

verification:
  "The instrument must be BUILT before the policy is ratified (R16:
   detector-first — check built 2026-08-15 before rule declared, precedent
   IMPL-WITH-DESIGN). Gates:
     - checks/classification-valid pass → exit 0 (all docs in canonical
       category); fail → exit 1 (negative control discriminates)
     - dir-schema-valid pass → exit 0 (schema matches tree)
     - archive-index-valid pass → exit 0 (archive/ fully indexed)
     - no orphan .vsm under docs/spec_revision/ (census, not happy path)
     - every moved doc: vsm-1.2 (R18 — edited docs at canonical version)
"

⟦ /classification_policy_plan ⟧